  "verbalization": "Alpha-Arbutin is linked to Histone H1.0 through two distinct pathways. In the first, alpha-Arbutin targets CWR22R, which in turn has a target that interacts with Histone H1.0. In the second, alpha-Arbutin directly targets Annexin A1, which also has a target that interacts with Histone H1.0. Both pathways suggest that alpha-Arbutin may influence histone modification or binding through a common downstream effector. The evidence implies that alpha-Arbutin could modulate histone function, potentially through a mechanism involving the interaction with a shared target or a downstream pathway that affects histone assembly or regulation. The integration of these pathways highlights the possibility that alpha-Arbutin exerts its effects on histone H1.0 via a complex network of molecular interactions, possibly involving epigenetic modifications or protein-protein interactions.",
